  body: "# Compensation and damages in retained old-scheme guidance\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe retained
    PB and MDB material distinguishes prior compensation entitlement from actual payment and distinguishes the timing
    effect of damages on weekly allowance from the timing effect on death benefit.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\n\
    Read this within chapter 73’s expressly limited retained scope after 5 December 2012. The source distinguishes
    awards never received, other-disease compensation and before/after-claim damages. It is not a universal rule
    for modern IIDB, personal-injury compensation or bereavement payments.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 73333,
    PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8019b540f0b62305b892c3/dmgch73.pdf#page=5).\n-
    [DMG 73335, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8019b540f0b62305b892c3/dmgch73.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 73348, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8019b540f0b62305b892c3/dmgch73.pdf#page=8).\n\
    - [DMG 73349, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8019b540f0b62305b892c3/dmgch73.pdf#page=8).\n\
    - [DMG 73350, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8019b540f0b62305b892c3/dmgch73.pdf#page=8).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol11-ch73`:
    PDF `3b17129736cf09e79f9df7079d4a83c4c2b74676d356c2c92947ef6cb12839ba`; extracted pages `d3ddd9b78f348565850afeafbaecd17ef9937905318211d171770a38ceadd7a3`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:34.331056Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8019b540f0b62305b892c3/dmgch73.pdf#page=5
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/industrial-old-scheme-transition
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: These provisions are retained exceptions to the chapter’s post-2012 transition narrative.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch73/0003
      quote: "73001   WC (Supp) and PB and MDB will not apply from 5.12.121. Therefore, from that date,\n      \
        \  people wishing to claim for\n\n        1.       accidents which happened or\n\n        2.       diseases
        caused by employment\n\n        before 5.7.48 should claim IIDB under the normal rules2. Apart from DMG
        73002 –\n        73003, the only guidance being retained is on other compensation (see DMG 73332\n     \
        \   et seq) and death benefit (see DMG 73412 et seq).\n                                                \
        \                 1 WR Act 12, s 64(2); 2 SS CB Act 92, s 94(1) & 108(1)\n\n\n        People receiving WC
        (Supp) or PB and MDB"
      locator: DMG 73001
  - target: term/industrial-old-death-benefit
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source gives death benefit a distinct damages-timing treatment from a weekly allowance.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch73/0008
      quote: "73349   If death benefit is involved, the benefit is not payable if the damages are received\n   \
        \     before the claim is made."
      locator: DMG 73349
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch73/0008
      quote: "73350   A payment of damages received after the date of claim has no effect on the payment\n     \
        \   of death benefit. This applies even if the damages are received between the date of\n        claim and
        the date the DM decides the claim."
      locator: DMG 73350
